Node startup migrates executable contract metadata without a chain resync and advances chainstate to version 15, preventing downgrade even if migration is interrupted. Allow time and disk space for conversion. Inspection tools and clarity-cli refuse unmigrated existing databases; use `stacks-inspect migrate-contract-storage <chainstate-dir>` on a disposable node copy, or `--standalone <marf.sqlite>` for a standalone Clarity database. Retain the original for older binaries.
